# Owner-friendly UI (required)

Design for gym owners and staff who may not be technical. Every screen should explain itself
without a support call.

## Plain language

- Avoid jargon (RLS, slug, token, schema) in owner-facing copy
- Prefer "Save changes" over "Persist config"; "Homepage hero" over "hero section props"

## Help on every control

- Every actionable field needs guidance: `FieldLabelWithHint`, `InfoHint`, `HoverHint`, or concise
  inline helper copy
- Store reusable hint + recommendation pairs in `src/lib/brand-help.ts` (or domain help modules)
- Recommendations sit in muted `text-xs` below the label — one sentence, actionable

## Live preview for visible changes

- Settings that change the public or member site must show what visitors will see
- Use **`SettingsEditorShell` `stickyPreview`** + **`SettingsLivePreviewPanel`** + **`SettingsLivePreviewFrame`**
  (see `.cursor/rules/settings-live-preview.mdc`) — real homepage iframe, not mock chip strips
- Typography, colors, images, and copy controls include an inline or adjacent preview snippet
  (e.g. font size fields render sample text at that size; color fields show swatch + usage)

## Guidance without clutter

- One short hint + one optional recommendation per field — not walls of text
- Image fields: dimensions, aspect ratio, and where the image appears on the site
- Font sizes: show pixel equivalent and a live sample; support px, rem, and em
- Prefer sensible defaults and "Recommended" callouts over blank slates

## Reuse existing primitives

- `src/components/ui/info-hint.tsx` — `InfoHint`, `FieldLabelWithHint`, `SettingSectionTitle`
- `src/lib/brand-help.ts` — brand/settings copy patterns
- `ThemeColorField` — reference for preview + hint + recommendation layout
